title: verify_token_f refetches the JWKS on every rejected token
updated: 2026-10-25T01:13:33Z
---

`lib/Net/Async/Zitadel/OIDC.pm:179-195`: after *any* decode failure (`$@` true and no `no_retry`) the code calls `jwks_f(force_refresh => 1)`. Expired tokens, wrong issuer or audience, bad signatures and garbage all cost one HTTP request to Zitadel each, uncoalesced. A client that sends invalid bearer tokens can make the service flood its IdP; and when that refresh fails the caller gets `JWKS fetch failed` instead of the reason the token was rejected.

`Net::Async::Authentik::OIDC` and `WWW::Authentik::OIDC` refresh only on `kid_keys lookup failed` and at most every `jwks_min_age` seconds.

Done: retry only for an unknown kid, rate-limited; other failures fail the Future with the original error. Tests: expired token -> no second JWKS request; unknown kid -> exactly one. Fix together with p5-www-zitadel.

